an3.67:8.1 starts: delight in each other’s misspoken word,
an3.67:8.2 starts: slip, stumble, defeat.
an3.67:8.3 starts: Noble ones
an3.67:8.4 starts: don’t speak in that way.
an4.24:8.1 starts: “Whatever is seen or heard or sensed
an4.24:8.2 starts: and fastened onto as true by others,
an4.24:8.3 starts: One who is Such—among the self-fettered—
an4.24:8.4 starts: would not further claim to be true or
an3.67:9.1 starts: If wise people, knowing the right time,
an3.67:9.2 starts: want to speak,
an3.67:9.3 starts: then, words connected with justice,
an3.67:9.4 starts: following the ways of the noble ones:
an3.67:10.1 starts: That’s what the enlightened ones speak,
an3.67:10.2 starts: without anger or arrogance,
an3.67:10.3 starts: with a mind not boiling over,
an3.67:10.4 starts: without vehemence, without spite.
an3.67:13.1 starts: For the purpose of knowledge,
an3.67:13.2 starts: counsel that’s true:
an3.67:13.3 starts: That’s how noble ones give counsel.
an3.67:13.4 starts: That’s the noble ones’ counsel.
an3.67:13.5 starts: Knowing this, the intelligent
an3.67:13.6 starts: should give counsel without arrogance.
an3.70:39.1 starts: Yet they—
an3.70:39.2 starts: aren’t worth one sixteenth
an3.70:39.3 starts: of the eight-factored uposatha.
an3.128:6.1 starts: “On one whose eyes & ears
an3.128:6.2 starts: whose senses
an3.128:6.3 starts: flies swarm:
an3.128:6.4 starts: resolves dependent on passion.
an3.128:8.1 starts: Whether he stays
an3.128:8.2 starts: having gained for himself no
an3.128:8.3 starts: tranquility,
an3.128:8.4 starts: he’s surrounded by flies.
an4.28:7.1 starts: Having cast away all deeds:
an4.28:7.2 starts: Who could obstruct him?
an4.28:7.3 starts: Like an ornament of finest gold:
an4.28:7.4 starts: Who is fit to find fault with
an4.28:7.5 starts: Even the devas praise him.
an4.28:7.6 starts: Even by Brahmā he’s praised.
